  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "1484bef2-dd72-d62f-b9bf-890718230c06",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "927427f8-7dc7-8382-bfec-2e7cb0fc038f",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Giving Nature A Voice won the non-fiction TV Series category which featured submissions from countries across Africa. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The series, which has been broadcast during primetime on Kenya's NTV since 2017, has featured in-depth reports on Africa's most urgent environmental crises. From the threat posed by ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "plastic pollution to Kenya's coastline",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OJLH_gFDCu8&t=0s",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_blank",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", to how climate change is affecting East Africa's Great Lakes, to the need to conserve endangered species such as the black rhinos of Kenya and the mountain gorillas of Rwanda; Giving Nature A Voice has fostered public debate and mobilized action to defend East Africa's wildlife and environment.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Emmy Award winning filmmaker Andrew Tkach attended the event and spoke of the importance of documentaries on ecological issues .",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
